# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: entmake-duplicates-subclass-markers — validate-entity-dxf appends 100 markers the data already has
#+STATUS: DEFERRED
#+PRIORITY: P2
#+TYPE: bug

* Symptom

ENTGET of an LWPOLYLINE made by RECTANG (or by any ENTMAKE whose data
already carries its markers) ends with a second copy of its subclass
markers:

: ((-1 . <Entity name: 10>) (5 . "10") (0 . "LWPOLYLINE") (100 . "AcDbEntity")
:  (100 . "AcDbPolyline") (8 . "0") (90 . 4) (70 . 1) ... (91 . 0)
:  (100 . "AcDbEntity") (100 . "AcDbPolyline"))

The vendors list each marker once, ahead of its subclass's groups.

* Repro

: (command "_.RECTANG" "0,0" "4,2") (entget (entlast))

* Cause

drawing/source/entity-families.lisp, VALIDATE-ENTITY-DXF: for a registered
family it always appends (100 . base-marker) and every family subclass
marker at the END of the data, whether or not the data already has them.
The command-probe summaries never record group 100, so the vendor
comparisons did not show it. Found 2026-10-04 while building alref S6.

* Fix

Append only the markers that are absent. For fidelity, also insert them
where the vendors put them (AcDbEntity before 8, the class marker before
the class's first group) instead of at the end.

* Progress (2026-10-04, clautolisp 2.2.168)

DUPLICATES FIXED: VALIDATE-ENTITY-DXF adds only the markers the data lacks
(test validate-adds-only-the-absent-subclass-markers; RECTANG's ENTGET
checked on the built executable). STILL OPEN, lower priority: a marker the
data LACKS is still appended at the end instead of where the vendors put it
(AcDbEntity before 8, the class marker before the class's first group).

* Deferred (pjb 2026-10-04: "If we know all that is needed for the subclass
  marker position, then do it now, otherwise defer the issue.")

Not all of it is known. The entity-family registry
(drawing/source/entity-families.lisp) records each family's marker NAMES,
not which groups belong to which subclass, and the multi-marker families
need that boundary: ARC (AcDbCircle, then AcDbArc ahead of 50), TEXT
(AcDbText twice -- where the second goes), VERTEX (AcDbVertex /
AcDb2dVertex), ATTRIB / ATTDEF (AcDbText + AcDbAttribute*). No vendor
measurement shows the positions either: the command probes drop group 100.
To unblock: a probe that records the FULL entget (100 included) of one
entity per registered family on AutoCAD and BricsCAD, then a per-subclass
"first group" table in the registry.
